# Git governance (Retornatus)

Adapted from Spec Guardrails **Human-in-the-loop / git blast radius**. Structural gates enforce artifact quality; **git tiers** enforce what leaves the machine.

> Approving a Change or Contract authorizes **local** work — not share, merge, or publish.

## Tiers

| Tier | Agent may do | Requires human |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **0 — Local** | Branch (when useful), implement, tests, commit locally (code + `.retornatus/` memory) | — |
| **1 — Share** | Nothing automatic | Explicit ask: `git push`, open/update PR |
| **2 — External (owner only)** | **Never** | Merge PR, deploy, force-push, production data, **PyPI/TestPyPI publish**, **release tags that trigger publish** |

### Owner hard rule (this project)

- **Merge** and **publish** (PyPI / TestPyPI / release tags that publish) are **always** the human owner’s job.
- The agent **must not** merge PRs, create/push `v*` release tags, run publish workflows, or upload packages — even if it seems convenient.
- When release is ready: prepare notes, confirm CI green, then **stop** and hand off: “Pronto para você fazer merge / tag / publish.”

### Tier 1 (share)

- Only after the user explicitly asks to push and/or open a PR.
- Do not push “because the feature is done.”
- Prefer a PR description that points to Change id (`C-xxxx`), Contract DONE, and Evidence / verify status when available.

### Tier 0 (local)

- Prefer small, English commit messages focused on **why**.
- Commit `.retornatus/` canonical artifacts when they are the durable record of the work (Changes, Evidence, Learnings) — not secrets, not derived `index/` / `runtime/` (see `.gitignore`).
- Never commit `.env`, tokens, credentials, or API keys.
- Never use `--no-verify` / skip hooks unless the user explicitly requests it.
- Never amend commits you did not create in this conversation, or commits already pushed, unless the user explicitly requests amend and safety rules allow it.

## Session handoff

At meaningful stops (session end, Change ready for review):

1. Ensure working tree status is clear (`git status`).
2. Local commits for finished units are OK (Tier 0).
3. **Stop before push** unless the user asked for Tier 1.
4. State the single next human step (e.g. “revise PR” / “merge when ready” / “tag vX.Y.Z to publish”).

